## 9. Verification checklist

Run before spending money. Every one must pass:

| command | expected |
|---|---|
| `qaas targets` | root = `project/react-site` |
| `qaas doctor --target allaabdellawebsite` | `live_ui yes`, `live_api yes`, `ready`; BROWSER + GUIDE in "can work here" |
| `qaas validate` | `config ok`; FIXER writes column is **not** `api/app,web/src` |
| `qaas tracker-check` | `tracker backend: jira`, auth/project/permissions/issue-type all `ok` |
| `curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" localhost:5173` | `200` |
| `qaas run --mode pr-check --dry-run` | prints 8 agents, no API call |

---

## 10. Troubleshooting

| symptom | cause | fix |
|---|---|---|
| **0 tickets filed** | REPRODUCER couldn't write evidence | `root:` is wrong. Check `qaas targets`. |
| `write refused: … outside sandbox` | write_paths are target-relative and don't match | edit `.qaas/config/agents/<agent>.yaml` |
| **BROWSER never runs** | `live_ui: no` | set `mode: external` + `web_url`; start the dev server |
| `stopped early: wall-clock cap` | mode ran out of time | raise `max_wall_clock_s` in system.yaml |
| `tracker backend: local` | `QAAS_TRACKER` not set | add it to `.qaas/.env` |
| `Bash is not in X's allowlist` | **working as designed** — discovery agents are read-only | nothing |
| `cannot be parsed as a shell command` | agent sent unbalanced quotes | harmless; it retries |
| **Security findings missing** | `JIRA_SECURITY_PROJECT_KEY` unset | set it, or read them as escalations |
| `cannot move X to 'in_review'` | that status doesn't exist in QAAS | add "In Review" to the Jira workflow |
| `--dry-run` seems ignored | flag landed on a second line | re-type it as one line |

---

## 11. Mental model

```
 MAPPER ─► the system map (everything downstream reads it)
    │
    ├─► ARCHITECT, API, BROWSER, DBA, AUDITOR, SOCKET, GUIDE, LOAD   (discovery, read-only)
    │        └─► DefectEnvelope  ── needs evidence or it is HELD, not filed
    │
    ├─► REPRODUCER  ─► minimises + commits a failing test to qa/repro/*
    │
    ├─► TRIAGE      ─► dedupes by fingerprint, scores, FILES the ticket   (Backlog)
    │
    ├─► FIXER       ─► minimal fix on fix/*, opens a DRAFT PR             (In Progress)
    ├─► REVIEWER    ─► APPROVE / REQUEST_CHANGES / ESCALATE  (≤2 round trips)
    ├─► VERIFIER    ─► re-runs the failing test → VERIFIED                (Done)
    │
    └─► REPORTER    ─► what was found, what recurred, what it couldn't reach
```

- **ROUTER is Python, not an agent.** It owns phase order, concurrency, budget
  and loop breakers — a model cannot enforce a budget it is itself spending.
- **The Jira board is shared memory + work queue + audit trail** — a blackboard
  system. Agents never talk to each other; they coordinate through the board.
- **Done ≠ shipped.** It means a reviewed fix exists on a branch and the failing
  test passes. Merging is always yours.
